WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.832
On this slide, we are focusing on a function with no parameters.

00:00:03.832 --> 00:00:08.627
Start with the meaning of the idea before worrying about the exact syntax.

00:00:08.627 --> 00:00:14.992
Ask what information is going in, what Python is doing with it, and what result should come out.

00:00:14.992 --> 00:00:19.107
A parameter is the placeholder name in the function definition.

00:00:19.107 --> 00:00:25.287
An argument is the actual value supplied when the function is called.

00:00:25.287 --> 00:00:26.792
Before clicking Run, predict the output.

00:00:26.792 --> 00:00:32.942
Then run the cell, inspect the result, and change one value or condition at a time.

00:00:32.942 --> 00:00:36.282
Rerun it and explain why the output changed.

00:00:36.282 --> 00:00:41.298
The goal is to understand the relationship between input, process, and output.
